<h2>Major Mistake #8: Company-Centric Copy That Ignores the Customer's Problem</h2>

<p>Read your homepage headline right now. Does it say something like "Johnson Plumbing: Quality Service Since 2003" or "Family-Owned and Operated for Over 20 Years"? If so, you are making one of the most expensive copywriting mistakes in contracting.</p>

<p>Homeowners do not care about your company history when their basement is flooding. They care about whether you can solve their problem, how fast you can get there, and whether they can trust you. Every word on your website should be filtered through the customer's perspective. Not what you want to say about yourself. What the customer needs to hear to feel confident calling you.</p>

<h3>Before and After: Homepage Headlines</h3>

<p>Here is how company-centric copy transforms into customer-centric copy:</p>

