<h2>Common Mistake #12: Treating Your Website Like a Digital Brochure Instead of a Sales Tool</h2>

<p>The final and most fundamental mistake is conceptual. Many contractors view their website as an online brochure, a place to list services and show photos. The top-performing contractors view their website as a 24/7 sales representative that never sleeps, never takes a day off, and never misses a call.</p>

<p>A brochure website has beautiful portfolio photos, a list of services, and a contact page. A sales-focused website has clear problem-solution messaging, trust signals on every page, multiple conversion points, dedicated service and location pages, fast load times, mobile optimization, and a clear path from "I have a problem" to "I just scheduled service."</p>

<p>The difference in results is staggering. A brochure website might convert 1 to 2 percent of visitors. A sales-focused website converts 6 to 12 percent. On 1,000 monthly visitors, that is the difference between 10 leads and 100 leads. At a 25 percent close rate and $10,000 average job value, that is $25,000 per month versus $250,000 per month.</p>

